{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 998244353;\n    \n    static long modPow(long base, long exp) {\n        long res = 1;\n        base %= MOD;\n        for (; exp > 0; exp >>= 1) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) res = (res * base) % MOD;\n            base = (base * base) % MOD;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n    \n    static long[] fact;\n    \n    static long binomial(int n, int k) {\n        if (k < 0 || k > n) return 0;\n        long num = fact[n];\n        long den = (fact[n - k] * fact[k]) % MOD;\n        return (num * modPow(den, MOD - 2)) % MOD;\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        \n        fact = new long[200001];\n        fact[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i < fact.length; ++i) {\n            fact[i] = (fact[i - 1] * i) % MOD;\n        }\n        \n        String[] parts = in.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(parts[0]);\n        long k = Long.parseLong(parts[1]);\n        \n        if (k >= n) {\n            out.println(0);\n            out.flush();\n            return;\n        }\n        if (k == 0) {\n            out.println(fact[n]);\n            out.flush();\n            return;\n        }\n        if (k == n - 1) {\n            out.println(2 * n);\n            out.flush();\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        int filled = n - (int)k;\n        long colChoice = binomial(n, filled);\n        \n        long result = 0;\n        for (int empty = 0; empty <= filled; ++empty) {\n            long choose = binomial(filled, empty);\n            long fill = modPow(filled - empty, n);\n            long term = (choose * fill) % MOD;\n            if (empty % 2 == 1) term = (MOD - term) % MOD;\n            result = (result + term) % MOD;\n        }\n        \n        result = (result * colChoice) % MOD;\n        result = (result * 2) % MOD;\n        \n        out.println(result);\n        out.flush();\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 998244353\n\ndef mod_pow(base, exp):\n    res = 1\n    base %= MOD\n    while exp > 0:\n        if exp & 1:\n            res = (res * base) % MOD\n        base = (base * base) % MOD\n        exp >>= 1\n    return res\n\nfact = [0] * 200001\n\ndef binomial(n, k):\n    if k < 0 or k > n:\n        return 0\n    num = fact[n]\n    den = (fact[n - k] * fact[k]) % MOD\n    return (num * mod_pow(den, MOD - 2)) % MOD\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    parts = input_data[0].split()\n    n = int(parts[0])\n    k = int(parts[1])\n    \n    fact[0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, 200001):\n        fact[i] = (fact[i - 1] * i) % MOD\n    \n    if k >= n:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    if k == 0:\n        print(fact[n])\n        return\n    if k == n - 1: